# Summary
Introduced. The new volatile Raft heartbeat overlay is not consistently promoted into durable fencing state for all commands that depend on the active primary lease. The patch handles metadata-transfer fences specially, but misses generic placement and availability transitions that also derive previous_primary_lease from the active primary.
Heartbeat renewals can now be applied only to a Raft leader-local overlay when the committed lease horizon covers them. Later commands are pre-applied to that overlay and the overlay is rebased after the durable Raft command commits, but the command actually written to Raft is usually unchanged and is applied by followers/restarts against the durable snapshot. Only FencePgForMetadataTransfer is explicitly rewritten to carry the live source lease deadline. Other commands that move an Active PG into Peering, such as SetPgActingSet and MarkNodeAvailability/mark_pgs_peering_for_nodes, still capture previous_primary_lease from the durable snapshot's node.lease_deadline_ms. If the active primary's latest lease exists only in the volatile overlay, the durable command stores an older previous-primary deadline. A subsequent restart or leadership transfer drops the overlay, so peering completion can be allowed after the stale durable deadline instead of the longer lease actually granted to the old primary. Under failover/reconfiguration conditions this can authorize a successor primary while the old primary still believes it has a valid serving lease, risking split-brain writes and object metadata/data corruption.

# Resolution
Fixed by [`41d81e90`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/41d81e90) (`Persist volatile Raft lease fences`).

The Raft authority now detects heartbeat lease deadlines that have advanced only in the leader-local overlay and commits a `PromoteNodeHeartbeatLeases` entry before submitting a durable command that could consume those deadlines. Promotion copies the acknowledged deadlines into replicated state, so placement, availability, expiry, peering, and metadata-transfer commands derive previous-primary fences from the same lease deadlines acknowledged to storage nodes and frontends. Followers, leadership changes, and restart replay therefore retain the conservative fence instead of reverting to the older durable deadline.

The promotion command is fail-closed and deterministic. It is bound to the current committed lease-horizon authority and Raft term, requires a nonempty strictly ordered node list, checks node identity and incarnation, rejects deadline regression and deadlines beyond the committed horizon, and updates only durable heartbeat lease deadlines. If promotion commits but the requested command later rejects, fails, or is interrupted by a crash or leadership change, retaining the longer deadline is conservative and prevents early successor activation. Command codec version 10 adds the replicated form with malformed and noncanonical decode coverage.

Regression coverage verifies that a volatile renewal is promoted before an acting-set transition, the resulting previous-primary fence uses the acknowledged deadline, wrong-incarnation promotion rejects without mutation, rejected follow-up commands do not discard the promoted fence, and stale Raft authority terms reject deterministically while advancing the applied cursor. The complete workspace validation for the fix passed all 6,816 nextest tests, workspace clippy with `-D warnings`, formatting, and `git diff --check`.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm volatile heartbeat can advance node lease only in leader-local overlay without durable Raft log progress.
- [x] Confirm Raft submission rewrites only metadata-transfer fence commands and leaves generic placement/availability commands unchanged.
- [x] Confirm `SetPgActingSet` computes and persists `previous_primary_lease` from the snapshot it is applied against, so durable replay uses stale `node.lease_deadline_ms`.
- [x] Demonstrate a durable/restart replay snapshot stores an older previous-primary deadline than the live overlay for the same command.
- [x] Demonstrate security impact: at a time after the stale durable fence but before the real volatile lease, successor activation succeeds in durable replay state while the live-overlay state still rejects it.
## Report
Validated the finding with a targeted Rust unit-test PoC plus an LLDB trace. Key code evidence: `apply_covered_volatile_heartbeat` accepts covered heartbeats into a volatile snapshot and restores `max_committed_timestamp_ms` without durable progress (`crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:2044-2076`). In Raft submission, the overlay is used only for `bind_metadata_transfer_fence_command`; non-`FencePgForMetadataTransfer` commands are submitted unchanged to OpenRaft (`crates/storage/src/control_plane_raft.rs:3880-3902`). That binder explicitly returns unchanged for all non-metadata-transfer commands (`crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:2079-2086`). `SetPgActingSet` derives `previous_primary_lease` from `active_primary_lease(self, record)` (`crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:3452-3461`) and persists it (`crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:3530-3534`); `active_primary_lease` reads `node.lease_deadline_ms` from the snapshot it is applied against (`crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:16888-16901`).

The PoC constructs a durable Active PG on node 1, then applies a covered heartbeat only to a volatile overlay extending node 1's lease from 2103ms to 7104ms. It then emulates the Raft submission path for generic `SetPgActingSet`: `bind_metadata_transfer_fence_command` returns the command unchanged, so applying it to the durable snapshot records `previous_primary_lease_deadline_ms=2103`, while applying the same command to the live overlay would record 7104. Command output: `durable_node_deadline=2103 live_node_deadline=7104 durable_previous_deadline=Some(2103) live_previous_deadline=Some(7104)`. Finally, at 3103ms, the durable/restart state accepts successor node 2 activation, while the live-overlay-equivalent state rejects with `PgPreviousPrimaryLeaseStillActive ... lease_deadline_ms: 7104`: `complete_at_ms=3103 durable_completion_ok=true live_completion_error=PgPreviousPrimaryLeaseStillActive { ... lease_deadline_ms: 7104 }`.

Reproduction command: `cargo test -p storage poc_raft_set_pg_acting_set_volatile_lease_not_promoted_allows_early_successor -- --nocapture` passed and printed the above divergent durable-vs-live behavior. I also ran LLDB non-interactively; it stopped at the PoC's durable `apply_control_plane_command(submitted.clone())` call and continued to the same successful test output, confirming the replay path under debugger. A crash/ASan finding is not expected because this is a logical stale-durable-state bug, not a memory-corruption bug. Valgrind was attempted but is not installed in the container.

